==============================================================================
(1) SEIDEL SWITCHING CLASSES OF GRAPHS, UP TO ISOMORPHISM
==============================================================================
   n   classes   A002854(n)   match   [= two-graphs on n vertices]
   3         2            2   OK
   4         3            3   OK
   5         7            7   OK
   6        16           16   OK
   7        54           54   OK

==============================================================================
(2) DOES EACH SWITCHING CLASS CONTAIN A UNIQUE EVEN GRAPH?
==============================================================================
  classical (Seidel): for n ODD each switching class has exactly one even graph.
  This is the bridge to the repo's E_n.  Test it, and see what n EVEN does.
   n  parity  #classes  even-graphs-per-class (multiset of counts)
   3  odd          2   {1: 2}
   4  even         3   {0: 1, 4: 2}
   5  odd          7   {1: 7}
   6  even        16   {0: 10, 16: 6}
   7  odd         54   {1: 54}

  reading: value v with multiplicity m means m classes contain v even graphs.
